local patches:
  27b7dfb706dc650e5376d8b0d9dedbb1ffd2c655  allow `bind:this` and `bind:<name>` on elements under `experimental.customRenderer`.
             `bind:this` reuses `$.bind_this`. Other names compile to `$.bind_renderer(node, name, get, set)`, which calls the
             optional `renderer.bind(element, name, get, set) -> { update?, destroy? }` (types: `RendererBinding`).
             `bind:group` and bindings on svelte:window/document/body stay compile errors. A renderer without `bind` gets the
             runtime error `bind_unsupported_by_renderer`. `customRenderer={null}` components keep the DOM validation.
             `input`/`textarea` DOM init in RegularElement is skipped under a renderer.
             Files: compiler analyze+transform BindDirective.js, RegularElement.js; internal/client/dom/elements/bindings/renderer.js;
             client errors; custom-renderer/types.d.ts; tests/custom-renderers/{renderer.ts,shared.ts,bind.test.ts,samples/bind-*}.
             Design and upstream proposal text: docs/notes/fork-bindings.md.
